082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554401 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f58d9465-726d-5a95-9c7d-efc84289b65d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554470 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186553924 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554470 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186554058 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554470 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186554173 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554470 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186554277 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554470 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186554401 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554470 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554470 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554470 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186554277 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554470 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "64fabadb-f80e-5526-b940-02e3d7342ff0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554629 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186554470 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554629 #edb/ref 1069 "q-127310" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554629 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554629 #edb/ref 1071 "Use the flux form of Green's theorem to calculate the flux of the vector field\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=⟨{e}^{2y}+4x,\\,{x}^{7}-{y}^{2}⟩\n$$\n\nthrough the boundary of the square $-1\\le x\\le 0,-1\\le y\\le 0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554629 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e6203f86-9cf0-5174-84bf-8575e36ffa78" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554629 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j,$ and $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first derivatives on an open region containing $D,$ then the flux form of Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s={∬}_{D}\\text{div}\\,F\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhich is equivalent to\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dy-Q\\,dx={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y})\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ and the curve $C$ for this case are shown below.\n\n![](images/09/09acd3df62b333bdaeb7553599507d4dbad7412ef2770b00e8fc8855b38a774e.png)\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)={e}^{2y}+4x$ and $Q(x,y)={x}^{7}-{y}^{2}.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂x}=4,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} & =-2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can express the rectangular region $D$ as follows:\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y):-1\\le x\\le 0,\\,-1\\le y\\le 0\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem in flux form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s & ={∮}_{C}P\\,dy-Q\\,dx \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(4-2y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}(4-2y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}(4-2y)[x]_{-1}^{0}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}(4-2y)\\cdot 1\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}(4-2y)\\,dy \\\\  & =[4y-{y}^{2}]_{-1}^{0} \\\\  & =0-(4(-1)-(-1)^{2}) \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554657 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186554711 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554657 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "294740c4-a895-510b-b2f2-8fc11a1beb8f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554657 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186481405 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554666 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3daca5bb-72c1-504c-aefd-215eeb4c35f9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554666 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186424520 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554675 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186554657 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554675 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4ff89872-91e6-53c4-9d19-3490a585a972" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554675 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186554629 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554711 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186554666 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554711 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "989b214e-cc0a-554a-a40f-d6e57d83e034" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554711 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186424518 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554726 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186554675 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554726 #edb/ref 1062 #uui